### Measuring and Smoothing Analog Signals

Because ADC conversions measure tiny voltage steps (4.88 mV), small thermal ripples and supply fluctuations produce slight reading jitter (e.g. 511, 513, 512, 514).

```cpp
// Moving Average of 8 consecutive readings
int readSmoothedAnalog(int pin) {
  long sum = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    sum += analogRead(pin);
    delay(2);
  }
  return sum / 8;
}
```

